{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Overlapping test paths can cause an unrelated failure to be treated as confirmation of a regression."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Shared globals can make isolated tests interfere during targeted retries, causing false regressions or preventing real regressions from blocking delivery."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A registered credential embedded in a failing test filename can be persisted unredacted in the baseline cache."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A retry that hangs after being reported as quick can hold a shared test slot for the full check timeout, delaying other work."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A load failure omitted from the test report can disappear from implementer feedback until a later repair round."}]}